## Part 2: Backend Engineering Commandments (Cards 02 to 13)

### 02. Secure Your APIs (Auth & Authorization) 🔐
- User $\to$ Login $\to$ Auth Service (Verify credentials) $\to$ Access Token (JWT) $\to$ Protected API $\to$ Allow / Reject.
- **Includes**: Password hashing (`bcryptjs`), 7-day JWTs, strict RBAC (`STUDENT`, `ALUMNI`, `FACULTY`, `ADMIN`).

### 03. Never Trust Client Input (Validate Every Request) ⚠️
- Users can send: missing fields, invalid emails, wrong data types, malicious payloads.
- **Workflow**: Client Request $\to$ Validation Layer (Zod/Joi) $\to$ Valid? $\to$ Yes $\to$ Business Logic / No $\to$ 400 Bad Request.
- **Validates**: Request body, query parameters, route parameters, file uploads (MIME types, max size 5MB).

### 04. Build Centralized Error Handling 🚨
- Don't return random server errors or unhandled HTML crashes.
- **Standard Envelope**:
  ```json
  { "success": false, "code": "ERROR_CODE", "message": "Human readable description" }
  ```
- Handled by Express Global Error Middleware.

### 05. Database Design Matters 🗄️
- Good schema design, primary keys, relationships, B-Tree indexes, transactions, pagination, data consistency.
- **Question**: *"Will this database design still work when I have 10 million records?"*
- **Applied**: Indexes on `batchYear`, `department`, `currentCompany`; mandatory `limit=20` pagination; `Serializable` transactions.

### 06. Don't Hit Your Database Every Time (Add Caching) ⚡
- Client $\to$ API $\to$ Cache?
  - **HIT**: Return Data (<5ms)
  - **MISS**: Database $\to$ Cache $\to$ Response
- **Cached**: Public dashboard counts, directory filter lists, approved stories (5-minute TTL via in-memory LRU cache).

### 07. Protect Your APIs (Add Rate Limiting) 🚦
- Client $\to$ Rate Limiter $\to$ API.
- **Config**: 100 requests/min global; 5 requests/min on `/api/auth/login` to prevent brute-force attacks and traffic spikes.

### 08. Use Queues for Heavy Tasks (Move Heavy Work to Background) ✉️
- ❌ **Synchronous**: Request $\to$ Report $\to$ Email $\to$ Image $\to$ Response 😵 (2–5s latency)
- ✅ **Asynchronous**: Request $\to$ API $\to$ Queue $\to$ Immediate Response ⚡ (<50ms) $\to$ Background Worker handles Email/Processing.

### 09. Don't Deploy Untested Code (Test Your Backend) 🧪
- Unit Tests, Integration Tests, API Tests, End-to-End Tests.
- Developer $\to$ Automated Tests $\to$ Pass? $\to$ Deploy.
- **Goal**: *"Catch bugs before users do."*

### 10. Know What's Happening Inside Your Backend (Structured Logging) 📝
- When production breaks, `console.log()` isn't enough.
- Log important events: API requests, errors, slow queries (>500ms), login attempts, payments, critical failures.
- **Tools**: Morgan / Pino JSON structured logs.

### 13. Secure Your Production Environment (Production Security) 🛡️
- Never expose API keys, passwords, JWT secrets, cloud credentials.
- **Use**: Environment variables (`.env`), HTTPS, Helmet security headers, CORS restrictions, input sanitization.

